<div id="A9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Notes.</span> Overlap = number of overlapping nodes in the top-100;
Jaccard = Jaccard index between the two sets;
Spearman <math id="A9.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> = Spearman rank correlation between frequency-based and contextual centralities;
Avg PPMI = mean run-level inclusion rate for PPMI-based backbone nodes (top-100 by PPMI strength) among the 20 constraints selected per run;
Avg Cooc = mean run-level inclusion rate for frequency-based hub nodes (top-100 by co-occurrence strength) among the 20 constraints selected per run.</p>
</div>
<div id="A9.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A9.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Summary.</span> Frequency-based hubs generally did not align with contextual backbones; alignment was stronger for gpt5 and o4mini (with higher Avg Cooc), weakest for gpt4.1 and qwen; Spearman <math id="A9.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> was mostly negative and significant.</p>
</div>
</section>
